cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, its data or its results, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Jev vs the LLMs: an eDiscovery relevance-review benchmark"
authors:
  - family-names: Sexton
    given-names: Ben
year: 2026
date-released: 2026-09-27
version: "1.0"
url: "https://decider.tarcalc.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/abcdben/jev-edisc-eval"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A benchmark comparing TypeSafe AI's Jev with frontier generative LLMs
  (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google) and a fine-tuned open model on eDiscovery
  relevance review across four corpora (synthetic Veridian matter, Mallinckrodt
  opioid-litigation e-mails, CUAD contract clauses, TREC 2016 Total Recall /
  Jeb Bush e-mails), on quality, calibration, determinism, speed and cost.
  Code is MIT; author-created data and results are CC BY 4.0 (see
  data/LICENSE-DATA.md).
keywords:
  - eDiscovery
  - technology-assisted review
  - relevance classification
  - large language models
  - benchmark
